# Forms stack policy

When adding or changing user-facing forms, field state, submit handling, or form-field validation.

## Stack (required)

- **Forms:** React Hook Form only (`react-hook-form`). Do not introduce Formik, Final Form, or ad-hoc form state libraries.
- **Validation:** Zod schemas only, wired into RHF via `@hookform/resolvers` (`zodResolver`). Do not use Yup, Joi, or “validate only in `onSubmit`” as the primary form validation path.
- Prefer schema-inferred types (`z.infer<...>`) for form values when practical; keep schema as the source of truth for field rules.

## Docs (do not restate APIs here)

- For React Hook Form APIs and patterns, follow `@react-hook-form-docs.mdc` and `https://react-hook-form.com/`.
- For Zod schemas and parsing, follow `@zod-docs.mdc` and `https://zod.dev/`.
- For resolvers wiring, use `@hookform/resolvers` as already in `@package.json`; check its docs when the resolver API is non-trivial.

## Preferences

- Extend existing form/schema conventions in this project; do not add a second forms or validation stack.
- Zod outside forms (API response parsing, shared domain schemas) remains fine — this rule only mandates Zod **for form validation**.
